Playing around with creating a microcontroller Tetris clone.

Hardware: 
    Board: custom designed in Kicad. Manufactured by OSHPark
    Processor: Waveshare ESP32 S3 Zero Mini N8R8
                (https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0GV459V87?ref=ppx_yo2ov_dt_b_fed_asin_title)
    Display: Waveshare 240×320, General 2.4inch LCD Display Module
                https://www.waveshare.com/2.4inch-lcd-module.htm?srsltid=AU7gw4WnNeeqWn06D45OdX-GpwlfIWSpdMTAS1l7iwtigELVDS8mfyD0
    Buttons/switch: Amazon find
    Battery: 2000MAH single cell lipo. 3.7v
    Battery Management: Adafruit Micro-Lipo Charger for LiPoly Batt with USB Type C Jack
                        https://www.adafruit.com/product/4410
                        Plug in USBC in the back to charge battery. 

Case:
    A case design is under way and this will be 3d-printed. I'll uplaad .stl files when I work out the design. 
    
Notes:
    Code was built and uploaded to the microcontroller via MSCode/PlatformIO
    See platformio.ini for configurations. 
    This version has 2 configurations one for the 8MB Flash version and one for the 4MB Flash.
    Default if the 4MB version. Pick your profile at the bottom ob VSCode with the Project Environment

Code: 
    The code is hacked together just to get the main functionality working. 
    There may be, probably are, still bugs! 
    I didn't write any tests but plan to do so now that its all in source control. After a morning of tracking down a nasty bug its about time. 
    The code needs a lot of refactoring also. Updating the datatypes from int to uint16_t, uint32_t etc last week caused the bug! Needed 32 bits and changed it to 16 :(
    There a LOT of Serial.print statements. On a full production unit these would be pulled out and Serial not used at all to improve startup time

Play:
    Top button rotates piece
    Left button moves to the left
    Right button moves to the right
    Bottom button drops piece to the bottom

    When game has ended press top/bottom buttons together will reset. 

